== B: Theorem 7.1's 'iff' with wide clauses
  F = {~x0|x1, ~x1|x2, ~x0|~x1|x2};  proj F == Ch_3: True
  F is UP_1-usable: False
  F with the wide clause replaced by its contained prime implicate ~x0|x2 is UP_1-usable (a 1-hop TC-spanner): True
  ... replaced by the other contained prime implicate ~x1|x2 instead: UP_1-usable: False
  m=4, 400 random implicate theories (path edges + 1..5 random implicates, k in {1,2}): {'theories': 400, 'usable': 46, 'some_rep_spanner_not_usable': 169, 'all_rep_spanner_not_usable': 46, 'usable_but_some_rep_not_spanner': 0}
  m=5, 400 random implicate theories (path edges + 1..5 random implicates, k in {1,2}): {'theories': 400, 'usable': 0, 'some_rep_spanner_not_usable': 116, 'all_rep_spanner_not_usable': 9, 'usable_but_some_rep_not_spanner': 0}
